WEBVTT

00:00:13.583 --> 00:00:16.375
"Saturday June 27, 2026 San Diego
9 Days before the attack on the Ocean Turtle"

00:00:26.958 --> 00:00:28.167
Leave this to me!

00:00:37.167 --> 00:00:39.792
Time's up, huh?

00:00:39.792 --> 00:00:41.958
All teams, retreat.

00:00:41.958 --> 00:00:44.875
Move away from Grid 1-9.

00:00:44.875 --> 00:00:47.667
That would've been
the last prey for today, right?

00:00:47.667 --> 00:00:51.500
You sure you want to end on a loss, Boss?

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:56.125
Battling an irregular squadron like that
won't do much good, training-wise.

00:00:56.125 --> 00:01:00.000
We wouldn't want any negative effects
to carry over into the actual operation.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.250
Let's go.

00:01:19.458 --> 00:01:23.083
Mr. Miller. The men from the NSA have arrived.

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:25.375
Send them in.

00:01:25.375 --> 00:01:32.958
Mr. Miller, we'd like to hire you, Glowgen
Defense Systems, for a top secret mission.

00:01:32.958 --> 00:01:34.708
And the nature of the mission is?

00:01:34.708 --> 00:01:37.917
To seize the Soul Translation technology.

00:01:37.917 --> 00:01:40.000
What is that, exactly?

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:42.750
It was developed by
a Japanese company called Rath,

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:45.792
and it's a machine
that can decipher human souls.

00:01:45.792 --> 00:01:47.583
Souls?

00:01:47.583 --> 00:01:48.875
Decipher them?

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:50.083
That's right.

00:01:50.083 --> 00:01:53.083
Using this Soul Translation technology,

00:01:53.083 --> 00:01:55.667
Rath has apparently succeeded in
not only analyzing human souls,

00:01:55.667 --> 00:01:59.125
but in cloning them as well.

00:01:59.125 --> 00:02:04.042
Should this artificial soul,
code-name ALICE, be fully developed,

00:02:04.042 --> 00:02:06.167
it could be installed into
unmanned Japanese weapons,

00:02:06.167 --> 00:02:09.833
which could disrupt the balance
of military power in East Asia.

00:02:09.833 --> 00:02:15.458
The U.S. needs to take control of that
technology before that can happen.

00:02:15.458 --> 00:02:17.167
I see.

00:02:17.167 --> 00:02:20.583
So, tell me the specifics of this mission.

00:02:20.583 --> 00:02:26.542
There's a mega-float for research called the
Ocean Turtle, moored near the Izu Islands.

00:02:26.542 --> 00:02:28.500
We'd like your people to break into it

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:31.875
and obtain the Soul Translation technology.

00:02:31.875 --> 00:02:36.458
That will require a raid on a Japanese ship...
one of our allies, you know.

00:02:36.458 --> 00:02:39.625
We've made arrangements
with the JSDF top brass.

00:02:39.625 --> 00:02:43.042
Apparently, the JSDF isn't the
monolith it appears to be.

00:02:43.042 --> 00:02:45.125
Use whatever methods you want.

00:02:45.125 --> 00:02:51.333
Just remember that the U.S. isn't involved
in this mission in any way.

00:02:53.083 --> 00:02:55.583
Fine.

00:02:55.583 --> 00:03:00.083
I'll assemble the team,
and lead it myself.

00:03:02.875 --> 00:03:08.042
ALICE, your soul will be so sweet.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:42.042
"The Final Load Test"

00:04:45.667 --> 00:04:48.250
"Main Control Room Ocean Turtle
35 minutes after the attack"

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:51.542
Critter, you bastard...
just try saying that again!

00:04:51.542 --> 00:04:54.667
I'll repeat it as many times
as you want, Vassago.

00:04:54.667 --> 00:04:59.667
Listen up! This console is locked tighter
than a pile of dried turds.

00:04:59.667 --> 00:05:04.417
I could crunch the numbers on the laptop
we brought until you die of old age,

00:05:04.417 --> 00:05:06.583
and I'd still never crack it!

00:05:06.583 --> 00:05:09.583
You're missing the point,
you damned four eyes!

00:05:09.583 --> 00:05:14.042
You said we got locked out
because we took too long to break in!

00:05:14.042 --> 00:05:18.042
Hey, hey, all I did was point out a fact.

00:05:18.042 --> 00:05:24.292
For someone who hung back cowering
during the battle, you sure are cocky!

00:05:24.292 --> 00:05:27.375
Okay, that's enough, you two.

00:05:27.375 --> 00:05:30.708
There's no time to point fingers at each other.

00:05:30.708 --> 00:05:32.875
We have to consider our
next move now, all right?

00:05:32.875 --> 00:05:34.792
Yeah, but Bro,

00:05:34.792 --> 00:05:37.625
this guy needs to be put in his place.

00:05:37.625 --> 00:05:41.750
I'm satisfied with what
this team's achieved till now.

00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:45.167
Our only casualty was Gary getting grazed.

00:05:45.167 --> 00:05:49.917
And we succeeded in taking over the
control room, our primary objective.

00:05:49.917 --> 00:05:55.417
Yeah, but if we're locked out of
the control system itself, what's the point?

00:05:55.417 --> 00:06:00.500
Our ultimate target, the Lightcube Cluster,
is beyond that wall, right?

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:05.958
That's why I'm saying we need to
come up with a way to breach that wall.

00:06:05.958 --> 00:06:10.375
Still, those JSDF guys
won't stay holed up forever.

00:06:10.375 --> 00:06:15.250
Once the real soldiers come charging in
from this turtle's escort ship--

00:06:15.250 --> 00:06:19.875
I was told that the client and the JSDF
have a certain deal in place.

00:06:19.875 --> 00:06:25.167
Apparently, the naval escort won't make a move
for 24 hours after the operation's launched.

00:06:25.167 --> 00:06:30.458
So this operation's not just a burglary, then?

00:06:30.458 --> 00:06:33.875
All right. Now let's go over
the current situation.

00:06:33.875 --> 00:06:37.542
It's currently 1447 hours, Japan Standard Time.

00:06:37.542 --> 00:06:40.375
Forty minutes have passed since we broke in.

00:06:40.375 --> 00:06:44.500
Right now, we're inside
the Ocean Turtle's Main Control Room.

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:47.083
Although we've successfully
taken over our target facility,

00:06:47.083 --> 00:06:49.625
we failed to capture the Rath tech,

00:06:49.625 --> 00:06:52.542
and we've been locked out of the system here.

00:06:52.542 --> 00:06:56.292
Our next objective is to take over
the Sub Control Room.

00:06:56.292 --> 00:07:00.708
Brigg, do you think you can
cut through the bulkhead door?

00:07:00.708 --> 00:07:02.500
It doesn't look too promising.

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:05.625
It's made of cutting-edge composite materials,

00:07:05.625 --> 00:07:11.792
and it would be impossible to cut through it
within 24 hours using the portable saw we brought.

00:07:11.792 --> 00:07:15.333
Hans, what if we used C-4 to blow it open?

00:07:15.333 --> 00:07:17.917
I wouldn't recommend it.

00:07:17.917 --> 00:07:22.000
The chamber housing the Lightcube Cluster
is just beyond that wall.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:23.833
If we blast open the door,

00:07:23.833 --> 00:07:27.000
there's no guarantee that the contents
of that room would be left unscathed.

00:07:28.083 --> 00:07:30.792
The mission we've been tasked with

00:07:30.792 --> 00:07:37.208
is to find a single Lightcube out of a mountain
of them, and extract it along with its interface.

00:07:37.208 --> 00:07:40.292
We already have the cube's unique ID.

00:07:40.292 --> 00:07:41.542
Come on,

00:07:41.542 --> 00:07:47.292
this scrawny Four Eyes has been giving us
this crap about hacking into the Pentagon,

00:07:47.292 --> 00:07:50.958
and yet he can't even crack open
a flimsy system lock.

00:07:50.958 --> 00:07:53.375
Whoa, what a shock.

00:07:53.375 --> 00:07:57.792
I just got told off by a gamer
who's only fired a gun made of polygons!

00:07:57.792 --> 00:07:59.250
You bastard!

00:08:03.083 --> 00:08:09.083
Do you guys want to go back empty-handed,
and get jeers instead of a bonus?

00:08:11.542 --> 00:08:17.042
Are you incompetent enough
to be outdone by amateur techs?

00:08:18.042 --> 00:08:19.708
Then start thinking!

00:08:19.708 --> 00:08:26.167
Prove that those containers sitting on your necks
are filled with something other than oatmeal!

00:08:34.125 --> 00:08:38.458
The pressure bulkhead leading to the Lightcube
Cluster chamber can't be breached.

00:08:38.458 --> 00:08:42.875
Meaning that our only option
is to control the system from here.

00:08:42.875 --> 00:08:43.792
How's it looking?

00:08:43.792 --> 00:08:47.042
No chance of logging in
with administrator privileges.

00:08:47.042 --> 00:08:56.708
About all we can do is peek enviously at the
fairyland where the Fluctlights live in such bliss.

00:08:59.625 --> 00:09:00.583
Goblins?

00:09:00.583 --> 00:09:03.333
Hey, you've done your homework, Captain!

00:09:03.333 --> 00:09:06.250
Yeah, but they seem kinda big for goblins.

00:09:06.250 --> 00:09:10.500
Those are Hobs. They're Hobgoblins, I bet.

00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:11.833
Critter.

00:09:11.833 --> 00:09:13.208
Yeah?

00:09:13.208 --> 00:09:17.125
Are these monsters part of the system?

00:09:17.125 --> 00:09:19.125
Doesn't look that way.

00:09:19.125 --> 00:09:24.875
These guys have artificial souls
loaded into the Lightcube Cluster above.

00:09:24.875 --> 00:09:26.958
They have Fluctlights.

00:09:26.958 --> 00:09:28.833
Are you serious?

00:09:28.833 --> 00:09:32.500
These Hobgoblins have souls,
the same as us?

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:37.458
Do those Lightcubes all contain
goblins and orcs like these?

00:09:37.458 --> 00:09:38.583
Is our Alice one, too?

00:09:38.583 --> 00:09:40.875
Of course not!

00:09:40.875 --> 00:09:43.000
This realm called the Underworld...

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:46.458
...is divided into the Human Empire,
where normal humans live,

00:09:46.458 --> 00:09:52.500
and the Dark Territory that lies outside it,
which is teeming with monsters.

00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:56.250
It's pretty much a given that
Alice lives in the Human Empire,

00:09:56.250 --> 00:09:58.042
but since it's so gigantic,

00:09:58.042 --> 00:10:01.583
there's no way that we'll ever find her
by just peeking in like this.

00:10:01.583 --> 00:10:04.042
Come on, that's a total no-brainer!

00:10:04.042 --> 00:10:07.083
If that's the case, all we have to
do is dive into this Human Empire,

00:10:07.083 --> 00:10:10.833
and ask whoever we come across,
"Hey, do you know a girl named Alice?"

00:10:10.833 --> 00:10:13.000
Wow, we have a dumbass here!

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:14.375
What's that, bastard?

00:10:14.375 --> 00:10:19.750
Look, there are tens of thousands of people
living in the Human Empire.

00:10:19.750 --> 00:10:23.583
You really think you can
canvas them all on your... own?

00:10:24.792 --> 00:10:28.167
Wait. Hold on, hold on! Maybe it doesn't
have to be done by one person.

00:10:28.167 --> 00:10:29.583
I see.

00:10:29.583 --> 00:10:33.333
The accounts set up
to log into the Underworld...

00:10:33.333 --> 00:10:37.250
It's unlikely that they'd all be
Level 1 ordinary citizens.

00:10:37.250 --> 00:10:39.083
Isn't that right, Critter?

00:10:42.083 --> 00:10:47.458
For the Rath operators to log in and observe,
or else control it from inside,

00:10:47.458 --> 00:10:50.292
they must be set up with accounts
of all ranks and professions.

00:10:50.292 --> 00:10:53.167
Hey! How cool is that?

00:10:53.167 --> 00:10:57.833
In other words, we should just log in as a
general or president or some other big shot,

00:10:57.833 --> 00:11:01.042
and order them to smoke out Alice, right?

00:11:01.042 --> 00:11:07.708
I don't know, hearing you put it like that...
makes this idea sound really stupid.

00:11:07.708 --> 00:11:09.875
Dammit, no good, huh?

00:11:09.875 --> 00:11:14.125
They have some hard-core protection
on the high-level account logins as well.

00:11:14.125 --> 00:11:20.125
Looks like we can only dive into the Human
Empire with an ordinary citizen's account.

00:11:20.125 --> 00:11:23.292
Damn, what a letdown!

00:11:23.292 --> 00:11:28.542
Critter, aren't there any high-level accounts
set up outside the Human Empire?

00:11:28.542 --> 00:11:29.708
Outside it?

00:11:29.708 --> 00:11:34.125
But aren't the chances
of Alice being there close to nil?

00:11:34.125 --> 00:11:36.417
Well, yes, I guess so.

00:11:36.417 --> 00:11:41.375
But it's not as if the borders
are totally impenetrable, right?

00:11:41.375 --> 00:11:44.917
That's my bro! Thinking outside the box!

00:11:44.917 --> 00:11:46.250
In other words, you mean,

00:11:46.250 --> 00:11:49.500
go in as general of those monsters
and attack, right?

00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:52.208
That would get me more fired up, for sure!

00:11:53.542 --> 00:11:56.833
A-ha, found it, found it!

00:11:58.292 --> 00:12:00.792
All right! No password!

00:12:00.792 --> 00:12:02.125
Well, well...

00:12:02.125 --> 00:12:06.167
First, here's someone with
the rank of Dark Knight.

00:12:06.167 --> 00:12:10.458
His Object Control level is... 70!
We can work with that!

00:12:10.458 --> 00:12:12.708
Hey, not bad!

00:12:12.708 --> 00:12:15.000
That one's mine, all right?

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:18.125
Right, and here's another one...

00:12:18.125 --> 00:12:19.708
What's this?

00:12:19.708 --> 00:12:22.667
The ranking's blank,
and there's no level, either.

00:12:22.667 --> 00:12:25.167
The only setting is its name.

00:12:25.167 --> 00:12:27.958
Now how do you pronounce this?

00:12:27.958 --> 00:12:31.417
Emperor... Vecta?

00:12:31.417 --> 00:12:33.792
Emperor... as in ruler?

00:12:33.792 --> 00:12:35.042
On second thought, I'll take that one--

00:12:35.042 --> 00:12:36.333
No.

00:12:36.333 --> 00:12:39.167
I'm taking that one for myself.

00:12:39.167 --> 00:12:41.000
I won't argue.

00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:45.667
Okay, so you can take on the role of Emperor,
and I'll be the Dark Knight.

00:12:45.667 --> 00:12:48.208
Hey, I'm starting to get pumped up!

00:12:48.208 --> 00:12:52.250
Hey! Four eyes! Can we log in yet?

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:53.917
What's wrong, Critter?

00:12:53.917 --> 00:12:56.333
Is there some other problem?

00:12:56.333 --> 00:12:59.333
Maybe it's just something that's bugging me,

00:12:59.333 --> 00:13:03.583
but I'm looking at the data,
and this odd phrase keeps popping up.

00:13:03.583 --> 00:13:07.667
I'm not sure what it means yet.

00:13:07.667 --> 00:13:09.500
What kind of phrase?

00:13:09.500 --> 00:13:12.208
"Final load test."

00:13:14.542 --> 00:13:16.750
Um... let's see.

00:13:16.750 --> 00:13:19.708
"Sub Control Room Ocean Turtle
37 minutes after the attack"
As far as Kirito's condition
in the real world is concerned,

00:13:19.708 --> 00:13:21.375
"Sub Control Room Ocean Turtle
37 minutes after the attack"
like I just explained,

00:13:21.375 --> 00:13:23.958
things aren't looking too optimistic.

00:13:23.958 --> 00:13:28.750
That said, Kirito still remains
logged into the Underworld.

00:13:28.750 --> 00:13:30.333
In other words,

00:13:30.333 --> 00:13:32.875
even though his self-image has been damaged,

00:13:32.875 --> 00:13:38.792
his Fluctlight itself is still active,
and is receptive to various stimuli.

00:13:38.792 --> 00:13:43.458
He's lost his own soul because
he blamed himself so vehemently.

00:13:43.458 --> 00:13:49.750
If someone in the Underworld were
to offer him forgiveness, then maybe...

00:13:51.667 --> 00:13:54.250
I'll go!

00:13:54.250 --> 00:13:55.875
Ms. Asuna?

00:14:00.958 --> 00:14:04.667
I'll go into the Underworld.

00:14:05.875 --> 00:14:09.667
I want to go there and tell Kirito...

00:14:09.667 --> 00:14:11.917
...that he did a good job.

00:14:11.917 --> 00:14:15.958
To say, "I know you went through
so much sadness and pain,

00:14:15.958 --> 00:14:19.667
but you did the best that you could."

00:14:19.667 --> 00:14:23.792
It's true that we have one more vacant STL.

00:14:23.792 --> 00:14:29.083
But the Underworld isn't
exactly stable right now.

00:14:29.083 --> 00:14:34.292
Because we're about to enter the last stage
of the scheduled final load test.

00:14:34.292 --> 00:14:36.250
Final... load?

00:14:36.250 --> 00:14:37.875
What's going to happen?

00:14:37.875 --> 00:14:40.292
The Durability of the Eastern Gate,

00:14:40.292 --> 00:14:43.083
which divides the Human Empire
and the Dark Territory, will reach zero,

00:14:43.083 --> 00:14:47.000
and an army of monsters
will flood the Human Empire.

00:14:47.000 --> 00:14:50.167
If the humans had sufficient defenses in place,

00:14:50.167 --> 00:14:53.083
they would've ultimately
been able to drive them back.

00:14:53.083 --> 00:14:55.542
But during this last experiment,

00:14:55.542 --> 00:15:00.750
Kirito pretty much destroyed
the ruling organization, the Axiom Church,

00:15:00.750 --> 00:15:03.208
so who knows what will happen?

00:15:03.208 --> 00:15:10.042
Either way, we may have reached the point
where one of us will have to dive in.

00:15:10.042 --> 00:15:11.750
Once the invasion begins,

00:15:11.750 --> 00:15:18.250
it's possible that Alice, who's somewhere in
the Human Empire, could be killed in the chaos.

00:15:18.250 --> 00:15:21.083
If someone can enter
with a superuser account,

00:15:21.083 --> 00:15:26.917
transport Alice, under their protection,
to the World End's Altar,

00:15:26.917 --> 00:15:33.500
and from there, eject Alice's Lightcube
to the Sub Control Room.

00:15:33.500 --> 00:15:37.125
Isn't that what you asked Kirito to do as well?

00:15:38.208 --> 00:15:42.458
If he'd made it, then I'm sure
he would've pulled it off.

00:15:42.458 --> 00:15:45.375
Because he was right by Alice at the time.

00:15:45.375 --> 00:15:48.458
You're saying that several months later
in terms of internal time,

00:15:48.458 --> 00:15:52.500
it's highly likely that those
two are still together?

00:15:52.500 --> 00:15:55.083
I think it's safe to assume that they are.

00:15:55.083 --> 00:15:59.833
Meaning that having Asuna dive in
might be our best option.

00:16:00.792 --> 00:16:03.375
As well as the ability
to communicate with Kirito,

00:16:03.375 --> 00:16:08.458
whoever goes will need combat ability
to protect Alice in the Underworld, after all.

00:16:08.458 --> 00:16:13.500
Then we should have her use
the highest account level possible.

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:16.833
Well, the choices are endless, then.

00:16:16.833 --> 00:16:19.667
A knight, a general, a noble...

00:16:19.667 --> 00:16:22.917
There are all kinds of superuser
accounts to choose from.

00:16:22.917 --> 00:16:24.500
Hey, hold on a second.

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:25.208
What is it?

00:16:25.208 --> 00:16:30.833
Isn't there a chance that our attackers
could come up with the same idea?

00:16:30.833 --> 00:16:33.167
Oh... yeah.

00:16:33.167 --> 00:16:35.708
True, they're just as likely
to catch onto this method, as well.

00:16:35.708 --> 00:16:41.250
But they won't have time to crack the login
passwords for any superuser accounts.

00:16:41.250 --> 00:16:46.208
Their only option would be
a Level 1 ordinary citizen... that's it.

00:16:46.208 --> 00:16:48.333
What's wrong?

00:16:48.333 --> 00:16:51.458
Never mind, it's nothing.

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:03.375
"Everyone, I'm going to the Underworld, too.
I'll be coming back with Kirito,
no matter what, so don't worry."

00:17:13.083 --> 00:17:14.542
Are you ready?

00:17:14.542 --> 00:17:15.917
Yes.

00:17:15.917 --> 00:17:17.875
Anytime you're ready, please.

00:17:18.167 --> 00:17:21.708
"Monday, July 6, 2026 4:56 PM
Somewhere in Tokyo"

00:18:35.042 --> 00:18:38.167
Again... the guy from that day...

00:18:39.583 --> 00:18:40.083
"You have a message from Asuna Yuuki"

00:18:40.083 --> 00:18:41.625
"You have a message from Asuna Yuuki"
Asuna?

00:18:41.625 --> 00:18:41.833
"Yui"

00:18:41.833 --> 00:18:45.542
"Yui"
Sinon, there's something
that I'd like to explain to you all.

00:18:45.542 --> 00:18:49.125
Would you mind logging into AOL right away?

00:18:51.833 --> 00:18:52.292
"Sylvain"

00:18:52.292 --> 00:18:53.750
"Sylvain"
So you see,

00:18:53.750 --> 00:18:57.125
in order to repair Daddy's Fluctlight,

00:18:57.125 --> 00:19:00.125
Mommy has decided to dive into the Underworld.

00:19:00.125 --> 00:19:02.083
Big Brother...

00:19:02.083 --> 00:19:03.458
Kirito...

00:19:03.458 --> 00:19:08.000
Oh, he'll be fine!
He's always come back, hasn't he?

00:19:09.292 --> 00:19:13.000
So, is the Ocean Turtle all right?

00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:17.583
Aren't they under attack by some sketchy guys?

00:19:17.583 --> 00:19:21.167
Isn't there something that we can do to help?

00:19:22.125 --> 00:19:24.292
Well, about that...

00:19:24.292 --> 00:19:29.208
We might need to call on you for help later on.

00:19:31.458 --> 00:19:35.292
"Main Control Room Ocean Turtle
2 hours and 53 minutes after the attack"

00:19:41.417 --> 00:19:44.458
All right, let's do this!

00:20:04.958 --> 00:20:08.792
"October 30, 380 HE
Dark Territory Obsidia Palace"

00:20:11.292 --> 00:20:15.792
"Dark Knight Eleventh Rank     Lipia Zancale"
Knight Lipia Zancale has returned.

00:20:15.792 --> 00:20:18.333
Good work. You can have a seat.

00:20:18.333 --> 00:20:20.292
Yes, my lord.

00:20:21.417 --> 00:20:25.125
"Dark Knight Commander Vixur ul Shasta"
Don't call me "your lord"
when it's just you and me.

00:20:25.875 --> 00:20:29.458
Right, but officially, I'm still on duty.

00:20:31.167 --> 00:20:32.833
So anyway...

00:20:32.833 --> 00:20:37.417
What's this grave incident that you had
to send a familiar to alert me about?

00:20:37.417 --> 00:20:44.125
Right. The pontifex of the Human Empire's
Axiom Church... is dead.

00:20:46.500 --> 00:20:48.083
That immortal being?

00:20:48.083 --> 00:20:49.583
Yes.

00:20:49.583 --> 00:20:54.833
I also found it hard to believe,
so I spent a full week making sure it was true.

00:21:00.625 --> 00:21:02.167
This is our chance.

00:21:02.167 --> 00:21:03.708
Chance for what?

00:21:03.708 --> 00:21:06.500
Needless to say, for peace.

00:21:06.500 --> 00:21:11.000
Do you really believe that's possible, my lord?

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:16.083
Whether it's possible or not,
it's something we must do, no matter what.

00:21:16.083 --> 00:21:17.542
But...

00:21:17.542 --> 00:21:22.167
How do you intend to convince
the other lords, my lord?

00:21:22.167 --> 00:21:27.917
And would the Order of the Integrity Knights
even entertain peace negotiations?

00:21:29.417 --> 00:21:32.917
Regarding the Integrity Knights,
I believe there's a chance.

00:21:32.917 --> 00:21:39.000
If the pontifex has been defeated,
it must be old man Bercouli at the helm now.

00:21:39.000 --> 00:21:42.083
I can't stand the guy,
but I can have a dialogue with him.

00:21:42.083 --> 00:21:45.375
It's the Council of Ten that
could prove to be a problem.

00:21:45.375 --> 00:21:48.958
I know it sounds contradictory, but we...

00:21:48.958 --> 00:21:51.542
...may be forced to eliminate them.

00:21:51.542 --> 00:21:53.000
Four of them, at least.

00:21:53.000 --> 00:21:55.792
Which four are you talking about?

00:21:55.792 --> 00:22:01.000
Would it be both Goblin chiefs,
the Orc chief, as well as...?

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:03.250
The chancellor of the Dark Mages Guild.

00:22:03.250 --> 00:22:07.375
That woman's gotten her hands
on Administrator's immortality secret,

00:22:07.375 --> 00:22:11.000
and most likely desires to become
emperor herself someday.

00:22:11.000 --> 00:22:13.833
No way would she accept any talk of peace.

00:22:13.833 --> 00:22:15.417
But...

00:22:15.417 --> 00:22:18.417
...that would be far too risky, my lord!

00:22:18.417 --> 00:22:21.667
The leaders of the Goblins and Orcs
may not be our enemies,

00:22:21.667 --> 00:22:23.250
but as for the Dark Mages,

00:22:23.250 --> 00:22:27.208
there's no telling what tricks
they might have up their sleeves!

00:22:34.250 --> 00:22:36.250
Listen, Lipia.

00:22:36.250 --> 00:22:39.250
How long has it been
since you came to me?

00:22:40.667 --> 00:22:45.708
Um... it was the year I turned 21,
so... four years.

00:22:45.708 --> 00:22:48.083
It's been that long already, huh?

00:22:48.083 --> 00:22:53.167
Forgive me for putting you in such
an ambiguous position for so long.

00:22:53.167 --> 00:22:57.333
What do you say?
Isn't it about time you, uh...

00:22:57.333 --> 00:22:58.667
You know...

00:23:00.375 --> 00:23:04.458
Officially... became my wife?

00:23:08.417 --> 00:23:09.792
My lord!

00:23:09.792 --> 00:23:13.500
Sorry that I'm so much older than you...

00:23:21.792 --> 00:23:23.875
Emergency!

00:23:23.875 --> 00:23:25.667
It's an emergency!

00:23:25.667 --> 00:23:27.542
Th-The Throne Room!

00:23:27.542 --> 00:23:32.042
The chain sealing, it is shaking!

00:23:48.250 --> 00:23:52.150
Next time: "Dark Territory."
